      "body": "The published 0.1.0 artifact passed source/archive/consumer verification, but its unprotected main branch and mutable GitHub release did not satisfy the extraction release protocol. This PR records the 0.1.1 successor and closes those release-automation gaps.\n\nThe workflow now refuses an unprotected release ref before tag/release mutation, preserves the existing tag ancestry and release-record checks, refuses mutable/draft/prerelease existing releases, and checks exact immutable published state after publication. The predicates reject missing, malformed and multi-object API responses; 31 isolated fixtures exercise them without making online-state claims.\n\nAll three version-bound manifests and their handoff digests now identify 0.1.1. The handoff cites this PR and preserves its migration/change-set/NRM identifiers, original source baseline, exact consumer inventory and package/App test ownership. Production source and public signatures are unchanged.\n\nValidation: complete package CI passes at `e66aad1dd7daae05260bc1075d75320579aad35e`: [workflow](https://github.com/kumwe/localization/actions/runs/34115545120). 38 package tests / 350 assertions; 12 release-record parser cases; 31 release-integrity fixtures; maximum strict analysis/style/manifests; security audit; actual built ZIP installed as a no-dev dependency with 27 public symbols, standalone translation and real ServiceManager factory/alias/lifetime verification. The App strict Version 2 manifest loader also accepts the successor handoff.\n\nBefore merging, the maintainer must protect main and enable GitHub immutable releases. The setting affects future publications: keep 0.1.0 and its tag intact. No administrative endpoint, admin PAT, repository settings change, manual tag, merge or publication is included. The ordinary workflow token verifies the public release metadata. If protections were not configured, the workflow fails closed; it does not repair an already-published version.\n\nA fresh independent successor release attestation remains required before dependent package work or App adoption. See `docs/releasing.md` for the setup and verification order.",
