      "body": "Localization is embedded in Kumwe App, and locale negotiation directly depends on the host settings reader. This extracts the portable boundary while App retains authorization, persistence, settings policy, catalogue build/cache adapters and delivery.\n\nChanges:\n- Move 21 Domain/Application types and 2 ICU types to Kumwe\\Localization, preserving executable tokens against App 960ce8ec00cf724a7cae03e5ba09c4852c9ab54e.\n- Add DefaultLocaleProvider, a deterministic ConfigProvider and 2 explicit factories. Host-supplied operation context and non-shared translator/negotiator services prevent hidden global context.\n- Include 27-type API/capability/service manifests, complete member documentation, standalone/ServiceManager examples, strict extraction coverage/parity checks, package tests and release-on-record automation.\n- Commit the v2 handoff: 23 old/new mappings, 94 consumer files, retained host/test inventory and separate adoption instructions. KUMWE-MIG-2026-005 / KUMWE-CS-2026-005 / NRM-2026-006.\n\nValidation:\n- Final-head CI is green: https://github.com/kumwe/localization/actions/runs/34111672350 — complete composer check, current security audit and no-dev autoload verification.\n- PHP 8.5.10: 38 tests, 350 assertions; PHPStan max/strict clean; lint/member docs/architecture/manifests/executable parity pass.\n- The built 46-file ZIP installs as a dependency in a fresh no-dev authoritative Composer consumer; all 27 types load and real Laminas ServiceManager aliases/lifetimes resolve.\n- App's actual PackageManifests reader accepts the package as v2-manifested.\n\nNo App edits, historical aliases, releases, tags or merges. A human merge and independent release verification precede App adoption. ICU/date/timezone, scope-key and quality-parsing behavior remains compatible with the captured implementation.",
      "closed_at": "2026-09-07T10:42:45Z",
